{{- /* Global APM manifest (docs/adr/0026-agent-config-via-apm.md).
       `apm install -g` reads it from ~/.apm and deploys every dependency
       into the harnesses' user dirs (~/.claude, ~/.copilot,
       ~/.config/opencode). It runs from
       run_onchange_after_sync-apm-packages whenever this file or the
       agents/ package renders differently.

       - The own package is agents/ at the repo root, by absolute path:
         APM refuses relative local paths at user scope. That path differs
         per machine, so ~/.apm/apm.lock.yaml is local state and is not
         committed. Pin every remote dependency to a tag or commit here
         instead (`owner/repo#v1.2.0`). The Nix module sets `apmAgentsPath`
         to a writable copy: APM fails on a read-only local package, such as
         one in the Nix store (microsoft/apm#5544).
       - MCP servers: `registry: false` entries with `transport` and
         `command`/`args` or `url`/`headers`. Secrets only as `${VAR}`;
         the sync script runs APM with every such variable unset, otherwise
         APM writes the resolved value into ~/.claude.json.
       - Edit here, never with `apm install -g <pkg>`: the next apply
         restores this file and APM removes the package again. */ -}}
name: dotfiles-global
version: 1.0.0
targets: [claude, copilot, opencode]
dependencies:
  apm:
    - {{ get . "apmAgentsPath" | default (joinPath .chezmoi.workingTree "agents") | toJson }}
  mcp: []
